        a: "Yes — the standard is 1.5× to 2× your normal labor rate for emergency, after-hours, weekend, and holiday calls, plus often a minimum charge to come out. Speed and inconvenience have a price, and answering the phone at 11 p.m. is exactly what that premium pays for. The one rule is to name the emergency rate before the truck rolls (\"after-hours is time-and-a-half, with a $150 minimum tonight\"), never as a surprise line after the work's done — an ambushed surcharge turns a grateful midnight customer into a dispute by morning.",
