        a: "It depends on the customer. Per-visit billing (invoice after each cut) is simplest, ties revenue to delivered work, and handles weather delays naturally — best for new or one-off customers. Flat monthly billing averages the season into equal monthly payments, smoothing cash flow and cutting you to one invoice per customer per month — best for reliable recurring accounts. Seasonal pre-pay charges the full season upfront for your steepest discount, putting all the cash in the bank before the first cut. Offer per-visit to new customers and push steady accounts toward monthly.",
