        q: "How do I split a project into multiple invoices?",
        a: "Agree a milestone schedule before the work starts. For each stage define three things: a trigger (an objective deliverable like \"on approval of the design\"), an amount (that stage's share of the total), and a rough date. A common four-stage split is 25/25/25/25, weighted toward the front if the early work is heaviest or the client is new. Put the schedule in your contract, then send one invoice as each milestone is hit.",
